cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QSOL NEXUS in research, software, or architecture work, please cite the applicable tagged release."
title: "QSOL NEXUS: Model-Independent Cognitive Substrate and AI Council Architecture"
type: software
version: 2.0.0-alpha0
authors:
  - family-names: Slade
    given-names: Trent
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4515-9237"
repository-code: "https://github.com/QSOLKCB/QSOL-NEXUS"
url: "https://github.com/QSOLKCB/QSOL-NEXUS"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  An architecture-first model-independent cognitive substrate for persistent
  shared world objects, evidence, experiments, replay, and equal-vote AI
  Councils using a De Bono-style parallel-thinking process. The 2.0.0-alpha0
  milestone is documentation-only and does not yet implement provider adapters,
  authentication, Council execution, or the planned Python/Rust tooling.
keywords:
  - cognitive substrate
  - AI council
  - multi-model systems
  - model interoperability
  - reproducible research
  - provenance
  - replay
  - human-AI collaboration
